      "source": "https://api.fonteva.io/TechnicalDocs/ApexDocs/FDService/PaymentCredentials",
      "independentlyVerified": true
    }
  ],
  "OutOfScopeObjectFamiliesNote": "The Fonteva connector uses a COMPOSE pattern with the SalesforceConnector: it targets ONLY the Fonteva-specific AMS managed-package objects (OrderApi__* + EventApi__*). Standard SF CRM objects, admin, tooling, analytics, and community objects are either already covered by the SalesforceConnector or out of scope. Source: SOURCE_STUDY.md §7 Scope Decision.",
  "universalPK": {
    "fieldName": "Id",
    "type": "string",
    "length": 18,
    "note": "Every Salesforce sObject (including all Fonteva OrderApi__*__c and EventApi__*__c records) carries a system-generated 18-character ''Id'' field as its unique primary key. Used as the record identifier in the FDService ''Filter By Id'' query pattern (SearchRequest.id = ''Comma separated list of Salesforce Id''s to query by'') and in Salesforce sObject REST addressing (/services/data/vXX/sobjects/{SObjectType}/{id}). FDService wrapper classes expose it as the ''id'' property (camelCase per wrapper convention). Source: restapi.fonteva.io Search Request section + Filter By Id section; Salesforce Object Reference system field ''Id''."
  },
  "PaginationDefaults": {
    "FDServiceLayer": {
      "type": "Offset",
      "limitParam": "limit",
      "limitParamNote": "SearchRequest ''limit'' param = ''Number of records to return as maximum''. Source: restapi.fonteva.io Search Request table.",
      "note": "FDService SearchRequest supports a ''limit'' parameter for bounding result sets. No nextPage/cursor token is documented in the FDService REST reference. Full result sets are expected within a single response up to the limit cap. The connector may need to use offset-based or Id-cursor iteration for large datasets via the ''filter'' / ''whereClause'' param."
    },
    "SalesforcePlatformLayer": {
      "type": "Cursor",
      "cursorField": "nextRecordsUrl",
      "defaultBatchSize": 2000,
      "minBatchSize": 200,
      "maxBatchSize": 2000,
      "note": "SOQL query results via /services/data/vXX/query include ''nextRecordsUrl'' when results are truncated. Connector follows this cursor until ''done: true''. Same as SalesforceConnector. Source: Salesforce REST API Developer Guide v67.0."
    }
  },
  "IncrementalSyncCapability": true,
  "IncrementalSyncNote": "Salesforce sObjects all carry ''SystemModstamp'' (write-always update timestamp) and ''LastModifiedDate'' (user/system update timestamp). These are usable as SOQL watermark fields: SELECT ... WHERE SystemModstamp > {watermark}. This applies to all Fonteva OrderApi__*__c and EventApi__*__c objects. The FDService ''filter.whereClause'' param accepts URL-encoded SOQL WHERE fragments, enabling incremental queries through the FDService layer as well. Source: Salesforce sObject field reference (SystemModstamp, LastModifiedDate as system fields present on all sObjects).",
  "IncrementalWatermarkField": "SystemModstamp",
  "IncrementalWatermarkFieldNote": "SystemModstamp is updated on every save (including system-triggered updates), making it more reliable than LastModifiedDate for incremental sync. LastModifiedDate is the user-context alternative. Both are standard Salesforce system fields on all sObjects. Same as SalesforceConnector.",
  "WebhooksAvailable": false,
  "WebhooksNote": "The FDService REST API (restapi.fonteva.io) documents no webhook/callback endpoints. Salesforce provides Outbound Messages (SOAP) and Platform Events/CDC (Streaming API via CometD) for push notifications, but these are separate API families requiring a persistent CometD connection — not REST callbacks. The Fonteva connector uses pull-based incremental sync. Source: restapi.fonteva.io (no webhook section) + Salesforce REST API Developer Guide (Streaming API is separate).",
  "BulkOperationsAvailable": true,
  "BulkOperationsNote": "Salesforce Bulk API 2.0 is available for high-volume ingest/query operations (/services/data/vXX/jobs/ingest, /jobs/query). Salesforce Composite Batch API allows up to 25 subrequests per call (/services/data/vXX/composite/batch). The FDService layer itself does not document bulk endpoints. Source: Salesforce REST API Developer Guide v67.0 (Composite + Bulk API 2.0 sections).",
  "BulkAPIBasePath": "/services/data/v{version}/jobs/ingest",
  "APIVersioningStrategy": "url-path",
  "APIVersioningStrategyNote": "Salesforce embeds the API version in the URL path as /services/data/vXX.X/ (e.g. v61.0). FDService Apex classes also support a version parameter in getInstance(String version) but this is an Apex-level concept; the REST transport version is the URL path version. Source: restapi.fonteva.io endpoint paths + Salesforce REST API Developer Guide.",
  "ErrorResponseShape": {
    "description": "FDService REST API error shape (HTTP status codes table from restapi.fonteva.io). The FDService returns standard HTTP error codes. No documented JSON error body shape in the FDService REST reference beyond HTTP status codes.",
    "httpStatusCodes": {
      "400": "Bad Request -- Your request is invalid.",
      "401": "Unauthorized -- Your session id is wrong.",
      "403": "Forbidden -- The object/record requested is hidden for administrators only.",
      "500": "Internal Server Error -- We had a problem with our server. Try again later.",
      "503": "Service Unavailable -- We''re temporarily offline for maintenance. Please try again later."
    },
    "salesforcePlatformShape": {
      "format": "array",
      "elementShape": {
        "message": "string — human-readable error description",
        "errorCode": "string — machine-readable code (e.g. MALFORMED_ID, NOT_FOUND, REQUEST_LIMIT_EXCEEDED)",
        "fields": "string[] — field names involved (present for field-level errors)"
      },
      "note": "Salesforce platform REST API errors are JSON arrays. Source: Salesforce REST API Developer Guide v67.0."
    },
    "note": "Source: restapi.fonteva.io Errors section (HTTP status table) + Salesforce REST API Developer Guide v67.0 (platform error shape)."
  },
  "WriteCapability": {
    "Create": true,
    "Update": true,
    "Delete": true,
    "Note": "FDService documents full CRUD for OrderService (GET/POST/PUT/DELETE) and write-only operations for EPaymentLineMapService, InstallmentScheduleService, JournalService, OrderPaymentService, RecordMatchService, ScheduledPaymentChargeService, SubscriptionRenewalService (POST only). Salesforce platform REST supports POST/PATCH/DELETE on all writable sObjects. BINDING per plan-manifest.json: ''bidirectional vendor; not pull-only''. Source: restapi.fonteva.io endpoint table + Salesforce REST API Developer Guide.",
    "FDServiceWriteServices": [
      "OrderService (GET/POST/PUT/DELETE)",
      "EPaymentLineMapService (POST)",
      "InstallmentScheduleService (POST)",
      "JournalService (POST)",
      "OrderPaymentService (POST)",
      "RecordMatchService (POST)",
      "ScheduledPaymentChargeService (POST)",
      "SubscriptionRenewalService (POST)"
    ]
  },
  "ConcurrencyControl": "none",
  "ConcurrencyControlNote": "Neither the FDService REST reference (restapi.fonteva.io) nor the Salesforce platform REST API document ETag, version, If-Match, or If-Unmodified-Since optimistic locking headers for standard sObject CRUD. Salesforce uses field-level audit stamps (SystemModstamp/LastModifiedDate) but no HTTP-level CAS mechanism is documented for these endpoints. Source: restapi.fonteva.io (no ETag/version headers) + Salesforce REST API Developer Guide v67.0.",
  "DeleteSemantics": "hard",
  "DeleteSemanticsNote": "Salesforce sObject DELETE (/services/data/vXX/sobjects/{SObjectType}/{id}) performs a hard delete by default — records go to the Recycle Bin and are purged after 15 days. The FDService OrderService DELETE documents removal of Order records. No tombstone / archived flag pattern is documented for FDService or standard Salesforce sObject DELETE for these managed-package objects. Salesforce provides a separate ''sObject Get Deleted'' endpoint for tracking recently deleted IDs. Source: restapi.fonteva.io OrderService DELETE + Salesforce REST API Developer Guide v67.0 sObject Get Deleted.",
  "DefaultSyncDirection": "Pull",
  "DefaultSyncDirectionNote": "Pull (read-only) default per MetadataWriter discipline. Bidirectional requires sandbox validation against the customer''s Salesforce org. Write operations against Fonteva AMS data (Orders, Subscriptions, Payments) carry financial risk and must be validated explicitly.",
  "DefaultConflictResolution": "DestWins",
  "DefaultConflictResolutionNote": "ConcurrencyControl=none means no ETag/version for MostRecent policy. DestWins (last-write-wins to destination) is the safe default when bidirectional is later enabled, matching Salesforce''s own last-write-wins semantics on standard PATCH.",
  "CustomFieldMarkerPattern": "{namespace}__{FieldName}__c",
  "CustomFieldMarkerPatternNote": "Fonteva custom fields follow Salesforce managed-package naming: {namespace}__{FieldName}__c. OrderApi fields: orderapi__{FieldName}__c. EventApi fields: eventapi__{FieldName}__c. Customer org custom fields on standard sObjects: {fieldname}__c (no namespace). Source: SOURCE_STUDY.md § Patterns: ''All Fonteva custom fields use orderapi__ or eventapi__ as the Salesforce package namespace prefix when accessed via Salesforce REST API directly.''",
  "CustomObjectMarkerPattern": "{Namespace}__{ObjectName}__c",
  "CustomObjectMarkerPatternNote": "Fonteva custom sObjects follow Salesforce managed-package naming: OrderApi__{ObjectName}__c and EventApi__{ObjectName}__c. Customer-added custom objects would be {Name}__c (no namespace prefix). Source: SOURCE_STUDY.md § Vendor Context.",
  "FDServiceSearchRequestNote": "FDService GET endpoints accept SearchRequest parameters: (1) ''id'' — comma-separated Salesforce Ids to filter by; (2) ''filter'' (also documented as ''whereClause'') — URL-encoded SOQL WHERE fragment for arbitrary filtering; (3) ''fields'' — comma-separated field API names to return; (4) ''sort'' — comma-separated field API names to sort by; (5) ''sorDir'' — sort direction; (6) ''limit'' — max records. Source: restapi.fonteva.io Search Request section.",
  "FDServiceCamelCaseConvention": "FDService wrapper properties use camelCase. The mapping to underlying sObject field is: convert camelCase to underscore_case and append ''__c'' + namespace prefix. e.g. wrapper ''subscriptionPlan'' → sObject ''OrderApi__Subscription_Plan__c''. Source: SOURCE_STUDY.md § Patterns: ''camelCase ↔ sObject field mapping''.",
  "DiscoverObjectsMechanism": "Runtime discovery via GET /services/data/v{version}/sobjects/ (Salesforce Describe Global endpoint), filtered to objects whose API name starts with ''OrderApi__'' or ''EventApi__''. Returns queryable, createable, updateable, deletable capability flags per object. Source: Salesforce REST API Developer Guide + SOURCE_STUDY.md §7.",
  "DiscoverFieldsMechanism": "Runtime discovery via GET /services/data/v{version}/sobjects/{SObjectType}/describe (Salesforce sObject Describe endpoint). Returns full field metadata: name, label, type, length, precision, scale, nillable, createable, updateable, filterable, sortable, defaultedOnCreate, idLookup, referenceTo. Source: Salesforce REST API Developer Guide.",
  "DiscoveryIsAuthoritative": true,
  "DiscoveryIsAuthoritativeRationale": "The Salesforce Describe Global endpoint (/services/data/vXX/sobjects/) returns the COMPLETE set of sObjects accessible to the authenticated user. Filtering to OrderApi__* + EventApi__* gives the complete Fonteva AMS object set. Absence on a refresh means the object is genuinely unavailable (uninstalled package, permission change). Deactivation is safe. Source: SOURCE_STUDY.md I7 + SalesforceConnector.DiscoveryIsAuthoritative.",
  "WrapperToSObjectNamingNotes": [
    {
      "object": "Term",
      "sObject": "OrderApi__Renewal__c",
      "note": "The FDService `Term` wrapper class maps to the Salesforce sObject OrderApi__Renewal__c (a membership term/renewal record). The wrapper class name (Term) differs from the backing sObject API name (Renewal__c); the emitted IO is correct and in-scope.",
      "source": "https://api.fonteva.io/TechnicalDocs/ApexDocs/FDService/Term"
    },
    {
      "object": "EventChatterGroup",
      "sObject": "EventApi__Event_Chatter_Groups__c",
      "note": "The singular FDService `EventChatterGroup` wrapper class maps to the PLURAL Salesforce sObject EventApi__Event_Chatter_Groups__c. The singular-vs-plural difference is a vendor naming convention; the emitted IO is correct and in-scope.",
      "source": "https://api.fonteva.io/TechnicalDocs/ApexDocs/FDService/EventChatterGroup"
    }
  ]
}' EXEC [__mj].spCreateIntegration @Name = @Name_a485f5e2,
